The orders library of `--decreases-orders` (`Std.Termination.Orders`) gains the multiset (Dershowitz-Manna) order: `MultisetOf(r)` orders multisets over any relation `r` proved well-founded, so that one element may be exchanged for finitely many smaller ones, as VeriFast's bags of call permission levels are. The library proves the order well-founded, with no new axiom, and transitive when `r` is; `MultisetReplace` and `MultisetReplaceOne` prove a step, and `MultisetRel(r)` lets multiset orders nest. It may be used in ordinary `decreases` clauses and, under `--modular-termination`, in `decreases {:global}` bounds, where the library's multiset functions and lemmas count as applications of the relation they are given. Programs without `--decreases-orders` are unaffected. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211.
